        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 57-year-old male admitted on 22/12/2017 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation without consolidation. Blood gases confirmed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests revealed mild systemic inflammation. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and closely monitored with pulse oximetry and regular vital signs checks. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. Patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided prior to discharge. Please ensure follow-up spirometry and ongoing COPD monitoring in your practice. Yours sincerely.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
